  "worked_solution": "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\u27e8-1,\\,3,\\,-2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,-3,\\,2\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)+\u27e81,\\,-1,\\,0\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{1}^{0}\u27e81,\\,-1,\\,0\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,-3,\\,2\u27e9+\u27e8t,\\,-t,\\,0\u27e9{|}_{1}^{0} \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,-3,\\,2\u27e9+\u27e8-1,\\,1,\\,0\u27e9\\text{\u00a0} \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,-2,\\,2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
